@startuml agent-builder-phase4-boundary
' ============================================================================
'  AGENT BUILDER - PHASE 4 (freeze create_agent)
'  The substance of this phase is a BOUNDARY, not new machinery: which tool owns
'  which part of an agent. Read the four columns.
'  Render (from this folder):
'    java -jar ../../../../plantuml.jar -tpng agent-builder-phase4-boundary.puml
' ============================================================================

skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "Segoe UI"
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam class {
  BorderColor #444
  ArrowColor #555
}

title Agent Builder - PHASE 4: who writes WHAT\nfreezing create_agent at the skeleton, so the open-ended schema stays with `write`

legend top left
  |<#C8E6C9> | **NEW / changed** in phase 4 |
  |<#FFE0B2> | the tool being MODIFIED |
  |<#E0E0E0> | unchanged - shown for the boundary |
endlegend

' ══════════════════ THE ARTEFACT BEING BUILT ══════════════════
package "agents/<id>/  — one agent on disk" #FFFDF0 {

  class "agent.toml  (SKELETON)" as SKEL #FFE0B2 {
    name
    version          <<NEW in phase 4>>
    description
    model
    heartbeat
    [capabilities]
    [subagents]
  }

  class "agent.toml  (EVERYTHING ELSE)" as REST #E0E0E0 {
    tagline / color / suggestions
    skills = [...]
    audience / google_account
    [app] title/mode/entry/public/public_tools
    [tools] allow / deny
    --
    **[plugins.<p>.tools.<t>]**
    provider / model / resolution / ...
    .. UNBOUNDED: any plugin x any tool x ..
    .. any knob. Cannot be enumerated as ..
    .. tool parameters, ever. ..
  }

  class "IDENTITY.md / AGENTS.md / HEARTBEAT.md" as MD #FFE0B2 {
    the three prose files
  }

  class "skills/<name>/SKILL.md" as SKILLS #E0E0E0
  class "plugins/<pid>/" as PLUGS #E0E0E0 {
    plugin.toml + module.py
  }
  class "ui/ , templates/ , data files" as MISC #E0E0E0 {
    index.html / app.js / style.css
    vendor/agentd-client.js
    templates/*.toml
  }
}

' ══════════════════ THE TOOLS ══════════════════
package "plugins/authoring" #F5F5F5 {
  class CreateAgentTool #FFE0B2 {
    name = "create_agent"
    __ params (FROZEN at the skeleton) __
    action / id / name / identity
    rules / model / description
    subagents_allow / heartbeat
    heartbeat_md / capabilities
    <color:#1B5E20>+ version   <<NEW>></color>
    __ does __
    writes the skeleton files
    registry.add() -> LIVE now
    <color:#1B5E20>+ hands off: says what is written,</color>
    <color:#1B5E20>  what is missing, what to call next</color>
    __ NEVER gains __
    <color:#B71C1C>app / tools / display keys /</color>
    <color:#B71C1C>plugin-tool wiring params</color>
  }
  class CreateToolTool #E0E0E0 {
    name = "create_tool"
    agent="<id>" -> agents/<id>/plugins/
    compile-checks + hot-loads
  }
}

package "plugins/skills" #F5F5F5 {
  class SkillTool #E0E0E0 {
    name = "create_skill"
    -> agents/<id>/skills/<name>/
  }
}

package "plugins/core_fs" #F5F5F5 {
  class WriteTool #E0E0E0 {
    name = "write"
    ANY file, ANY path
    .. the open-ended half ..
  }
}

package "plugins/agent-builder  (phase 3)" #F5F5F5 {
  class ValidateAgentTool #E0E0E0 {
    name = "validate_agent"
    catches what write got wrong
  }
  class ReloadAgentTool #E0E0E0 {
    name = "reload_agent"
    makes agent.toml edits live
  }
}

package "agents/main/skills" #F5F5F5 {
  class "build-agent/SKILL.md" as SPEC #E0E0E0 {
    the full agent.toml grammar
    .. what makes `write` viable ..
  }
}

' ══════════════════ OWNERSHIP ══════════════════
CreateAgentTool ==> SKEL : writes
CreateAgentTool ==> MD : writes
WriteTool ==> REST : writes
WriteTool ==> MISC : writes
SkillTool ==> SKILLS : writes
CreateToolTool ==> PLUGS : writes

SPEC ..> WriteTool : the model follows this grammar
CreateAgentTool ..> ValidateAgentTool : hand-off: "now validate"
WriteTool ..> ValidateAgentTool : checks the result
ValidateAgentTool ..> ReloadAgentTool : once clean, activate

note as N1 #E3F2FD
  **WHY FREEZE, RATHER THAN KEEP ADDING PARAMS**

  Look at the right-hand column: [plugins.<p>.tools.<t>] is any
  plugin x any tool x any knob. It is not a long list - it has no
  list. figure-creator's whole engine (Nano Banana Pro, default
  template, resolution, two vision models) lives there.

  Enumerating that as tool parameters is impossible, so a
  parameterised create_agent can never be complete. Every new
  agent.toml feature would need: a new param, a description
  rewrite, and a model that learns a SECOND grammar for something
  it can already express directly in TOML.

  The model already has `write` + the full spec (phase 1) +
  validate_agent (phase 3). Those three cover the open half
  properly. So create_agent keeps the half that genuinely needs
  code - the skeleton and, crucially, registry.add() - and stops
  competing with `write` for the rest.
end note

note as N2 #FFF3E0
  **WHY create_agent STILL EXISTS**
  It is not just file writing. It:
    * guarantees a VALID skeleton (correct TOML key order -
      top-level keys before the first [table])
    * refuses to clobber 'main'
    * registers the agent LIVE via registry.add(), so it is
      resolvable on the very next message
  `write` can do none of that.
end note

note as N3 #E8F5E9
  **THE ONE PARAM BEING ADDED: version**
  Not schema-chasing - a top-level scalar with real
  consequences: bundle installs supersede BY VERSION, and
  validate_agent already warns when it is missing. Every
  agent scaffolded from now on ships packageable.
end note

N1 .. REST
N2 .. CreateAgentTool
N3 .. SKEL

@enduml
